.TH DANBY-BASKETBALL 1
.SH NAME
danby-basketball \- trajectory and backspin of a basketball shot
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B temple/basketball
.SH MODEL
The ball leaves a two-metre release point under gravity, drag, and optional
backspin lift.  Speed and launch angle expose the family of arcs that can reach
regulation hoop height.
.SH DISPLAY
The spatial graph shows the shot arc; telemetry shows speed.  Tracks change
speed, angle, drag, lift, backspin, and gravity.
.SH SOURCE
.B /appl/danby/basketball.b
.SH SEE ALSO
.IR trajectory (2)
